WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.440
Cost it, price it, sell it honestly, then plan ahead.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.100
This is the video for module four of Natural Skincare.

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:19.040
Creams look cheap to make, because most of the jar is water. But emulsifying wax, preservative, packaging, labels, labour and laboratory tests add up quickly.

4
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:34.790
Many new makers copy other people's prices, and only later discover they lose money on every jar. The naira prices in this video are approximate examples for practice only. Use the prices on your own receipts.

5
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:47.200
Start with cost per gram. Divide what you paid by the grams you received. If 500 g of emulsifying wax cost 8,000 naira, that is 16 naira a gram.

6
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:58.730
Rukayat multiplies every ingredient in her 265 g batch by its cost per gram. The ingredients total 836 naira.

7
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:09.860
Then five jars with lids at 400 each, 2,000. Labels, 500. Gas, 300, and gloves and alcohol, 300.

8
00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:22.780
Her own labour, 2 hours at 1,500 an hour, is 3,000. And she sets aside 150 a jar towards laboratory tests, 750.

9
00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:39.820
The batch total is 7,686 naira, so each jar costs about 1,540. The ingredients were only about 170 a jar. Pricing at 1,000 because it is mostly water would lose money.

10
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:59.160
For a 40 percent margin, divide the cost by 0.6. 1,540 divided by 0.6 is 2,567, which she rounds to 2,600 naira. Then she checks what similar creams sell for nearby.

11
00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:06.130
Facial oils are the opposite of creams. There is no water, so the oils are the biggest cost.

12
00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:14.690
Jojoba at 90 naira a gram comes to 1,215. Baobab, 486.

13
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.740
Rosehip, 421, and vitamin E, 22.

14
00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:39.760
The oils total about 2,145 naira. Add the amber bottle, label, sanitiser, half an hour of labour and testing, and the bottle costs about 3,895. At a 40 percent margin, the price is about 6,500 naira.

15
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:53.090
If your price is far higher than others, look for safe savings. Buy jars and wax in bulk once your formula passes stability tests, and make larger batches so labour per jar falls.

16
00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:59.630
And count failed batches. If one batch in ten is lost, that adds about 10 percent to your cost.

17
00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.700
But never save money by cutting the preservative, skipping pH checks, or using tap water.

18
00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:22.650
Answer questions honestly. If a customer asks whether it will lighten her skin, say no. It is a moisturiser that keeps skin soft. If you have not formulated or tested it for babies, say you cannot recommend it for them.

19
00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:35.330
Give samples only from preserved, stability-tested batches, in sanitised, labelled pots. Never sell cream scooped into unlabelled nylon or reused containers.

20
00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:48.790
Confirm each order in writing on WhatsApp. Then check the money has actually arrived in your Moniepoint, Opay or bank app before you hand over goods, because payment screenshots can be faked.

21
00:03:50.040 --> 00:04:07.610
Your project is a product file: formula, data sheets, batch record, stability log, feedback, label and costing, plus an honest reflection. For example, Ifeoma in Onitsha has a lotion that passed 8 weeks of stability checks, and a facial oil that passed 12.

22
00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:24.780
In days 1 to 14 she continues the lotion test to week 12. In days 15 to 30 she sells the facial oil to 10 existing customers at 6,500 naira, and gives 5 labelled lotion samples for feedback.

23
00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:36.100
If 3 or more say the lotion is too thin, she makes version 1.1 with 2 percent more shea and 2 percent less water, and starts a new stability test.

24
00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:47.310
Then she asks two laboratories for test quotes, and lists her CAC and NAFDAC documents. Selling the lotion widely waits for the testing that makes it safe.

25
00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:59.570
To remember. Count packaging, labour and testing, not just ingredients. Price by dividing cost by one minus your margin. Never cut safety to cut cost.

26
00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.550
Answer honestly, sample cleanly, and confirm every payment in your own app.

27
00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:14.330
Now cost your own cream and facial oil, create honest listings for both, and assemble your product file with a dated 90-day plan.

28
00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.620
Continue with the lessons below.
